,"Call clients first"],"answer":"Duck, cover and hold"}]},{"id":"barista-common-l3-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-common-l3","title":"Customer Service Excellence Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-common-l3-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"What is the first step in handling a customer complaint?","options":["Defend the company","Listen without interrupting","Offer a refund immediately","Blame another staff member"],"answer":"Listen without interrupting"},{"id":"barista-common-l3-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Customer expectations are met only when the service is free of charge.","answer":false},{"id":"barista-common-l3-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The measure of how happy customers are with a service is customer ______.","answer":"satisfaction"},{"id":"barista-common-l3-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A customer is angry about a delayed order. What should you say first?","options":["That is not our problem.","I understand — let me check the status for you.","You should have ordered earlier.","Call again tomorrow."],"answer":"I understand — let me check the status for you."}]},{"id":"barista-common-l4-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-common-l4","title":"Working with Others & Time Management Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-common-l4-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which practice helps a team meet deadlines?","options":["Working without a plan","Setting priorities and tracking tasks","Avoiding updates","Doing everything at the last minute"],"answer":"Setting priorities and tracking tasks"},{"id":"barista-common-l4-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A task list should be reviewed and updated as work progresses.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-common-l4-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Arranging tasks from most to least important is called ______.","answer":"prioritizing"},{"id":"barista-common-l4-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A teammate is behind on a shared task. What is the best action?","options":["Ignore it","Offer help and inform the lead","Complain about it later","Take over without telling anyone"],"answer":"Offer help and inform the lead"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l1-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u1-l1","title":"Introduction to Coffee Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u1-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which coffee species is known for higher acidity and complex flavor?","options":["Robusta","Arabica","Liberica","Excelsa"],"answer":"Arabica"},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Roast level has no effect on the flavor of coffee.","answer":false},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The two main commercial coffee species are Arabica and ______.","answer":"robusta"},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"The processing method mainly affects:","options":["The color of the cup","The flavor profile of the bean","The price of the machine","The size of the grinder"],"answer":"The flavor profile of the bean"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l2-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u1-l2","title":"Coffee Roasting & Grinding Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u1-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which roast is the darkest?","options":["Light","Medium","Dark","Cinnamon"],"answer":"Dark"},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A fine grind is used for espresso.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"A coarse grind suits a ______ press brewer.","answer":"french"},{"id":"barista-core-u1-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"What happens when coffee is ground too fine for a drip brewer?","options":["It brews faster","It over-extracts and tastes bitter","Nothing changes","It becomes decaf"],"answer":"It over-extracts and tastes bitter"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l1-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u2-l1","title":"The Espresso Machine Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u2-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"What is the standard brew pressure for espresso?","options":["3 bar","9 bar","15 bar","20 bar"],"answer":"9 bar"},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"The group head is backflushed as part of daily cleaning.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The part that holds the portafilter during extraction is the ______ head.","answer":"group"},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Which routine keeps a grinder performing well?","options":["Washing it with water","Brushing the burrs and removing oils regularly","Running rice through it daily","Never cleaning it"],"answer":"Brushing the burrs and removing oils regularly"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l2-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u2-l2","title":"Dialing In the Shot Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u2-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"A shot that pours too fast and tastes sour is usually:","options":["Over-extracted","Under-extracted","Perfectly dialed","Decaffeinated"],"answer":"Under-extracted"},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Adjusting the grind is the main way to change extraction time.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The amount of coffee used in the basket is called the ______.","answer":"dose"},{"id":"barista-core-u2-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A bitter, slow-pouring shot suggests:","options":["The grind is too coarse","The grind is too fine","The water is too cold only","The basket is too large"],"answer":"The grind is too fine"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l1-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u3-l1","title":"Milk Texturing Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u3-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Microfoam is created by:","options":["Boiling the milk rapidly","Adding air, then folding it into the milk","Adding cream","Shaking the pitcher"],"answer":"Adding air, then folding it into the milk"},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Milk is usually steamed to about 60-65 degrees Celsius for espresso drinks.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The glossy, velvety milk used for latte art is called ______.","answer":"microfoam"},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Which milk is hardest to texture because of its low fat content?","options":["Whole milk","Skim milk","Oat milk","Cream"],"answer":"Skim milk"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l2-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u3-l2","title":"Basic Latte Art Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u3-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which pattern comes from pouring a steady stream while moving the pitcher side to side?","options":["Heart","Rosetta","Tulip","Swan"],"answer":"Rosetta"},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A clean, dry pitcher improves foam quality.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Pouring art straight from the pitcher without tools is called a ______ pour.","answer":"free"},{"id":"barista-core-u3-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Consistent latte art depends mostly on:","options":["Very hot milk","Controlled pitcher height and flow","A large cup","Stirring the crema"],"answer":"Controlled pitcher height and flow"}]},{"id":"barista-core-u4-l1-quiz","programId":"barista","lessonId":"barista-core-u4-l1","title":"Building the Beverage Menu Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"barista-core-u4-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"A traditional cappuccino is:","options":["Mostly milk","Equal parts espresso, steamed milk and foam","Espresso with no milk","Only foam"],"answer":"Equal parts espresso, steamed milk and foam"},{"id":"barista-core-u4-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"An Americano is espresso diluted with hot water.","answer":true},{"id":"barista-core-u4-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"A latte uses more steamed ______ than foam.","answer":"milk"},{"id":"barista-core-u4-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Why are standard recipes important?","options":["They slow down service","They keep taste and cost consistent","They replace training","They reduce the cup size"],"answer":"They keep taste and cost consistent"}]}]$q$::jsonb)
  where id = 'barista';

