iate when writing to a customer?","options":["Sarcastic","Professional and courteous","Aggressive","Overly casual"],"answer":"Professional and courteous"}]},{"id":"event-management-basic-l3-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-basic-l3","title":"Basic Digital Literacy Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-basic-l3-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which of these is an email application?","options":["Gmail","Excel","Photoshop","VLC"],"answer":"Gmail"},{"id":"event-management-basic-l3-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A strong password should be shared with co-workers so they can open your files.","answer":false},{"id":"event-management-basic-l3-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The key combination Ctrl + C is used to ______ the selected text.","answer":"copy"},{"id":"event-management-basic-l3-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"What should you do before opening an attachment from an unknown sender?","options":["Open it immediately","Verify the sender and scan it for malware","Forward it to all staff","Reply with your password"],"answer":"Verify the sender and scan it for malware"}]},{"id":"event-management-basic-l4-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-basic-l4","title":"Workplace Behavior & Professionalism Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-basic-l4-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"What does punctuality at work demonstrate?","options":["Reliability and respect for others","That you are overworked","That you dislike the job","Nothing important"],"answer":"Reliability and respect for others"},{"id":"event-management-basic-l4-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Personal social media accounts may be used to discuss confidential client information.","answer":false},{"id":"event-management-basic-l4-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The set of rules that guides acceptable behavior in the workplace is the code of ______.","answer":"conduct"},{"id":"event-management-basic-l4-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A colleague keeps arriving late. What is the professional response?","options":["Post about it online","Raise it with the supervisor privately","Ignore your own work","Confront them in front of clients"],"answer":"Raise it with the supervisor privately"}]},{"id":"event-management-common-l1-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-common-l1","title":"Workplace Communication Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-common-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which channel is best for reporting an urgent safety incident?","options":["A memo next week","A call or direct message to the supervisor","A suggestion box","A social media post"],"answer":"A call or direct message to the supervisor"},{"id":"event-management-common-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Incident reports should be written as soon as possible after the event.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-common-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The written record of what was discussed in a meeting is called the ______.","answer":"minutes"},{"id":"event-management-common-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"What is the best way to confirm instructions you received verbally?","options":["Assume you understood","Write them down and repeat them back","Wait for a written complaint","Ask a client instead"],"answer":"Write them down and repeat them back"}]},{"id":"event-management-common-l2-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-common-l2","title":"Workplace Safety & Emergency Procedures Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-common-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"What does OSH stand for?","options":["Occupational Safety and Health","Office Staff Handbook","Operational Service Hours","Organized Safety Help"],"answer":"Occupational Safety and Health"},{"id":"event-management-common-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Fire exits must be kept clear of boxes and equipment at all times.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-common-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Gear worn to protect a worker from hazards is called ______ equipment.","answer":"personal protective"},{"id":"event-management-common-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"During an earthquake while indoors you should:","options":["Run to the elevator","Duck, cover and hold","Stand near the windows","Call clients first"],"answer":"Duck, cover and hold"}]},{"id":"event-management-common-l3-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-common-l3","title":"Customer Service Excellence Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-common-l3-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"What is the first step in handling a customer complaint?","options":["Defend the company","Listen without interrupting","Offer a refund immediately","Blame another staff member"],"answer":"Listen without interrupting"},{"id":"event-management-common-l3-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Customer expectations are met only when the service is free of charge.","answer":false},{"id":"event-management-common-l3-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The measure of how happy customers are with a service is customer ______.","answer":"satisfaction"},{"id":"event-management-common-l3-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A customer is angry about a delayed order. What should you say first?","options":["That is not our problem.","I understand — let me check the status for you.","You should have ordered earlier.","Call again tomorrow."],"answer":"I understand — let me check the status for you."}]},{"id":"event-management-common-l4-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-common-l4","title":"Working with Others & Time Management Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-common-l4-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which practice helps a team meet deadlines?","options":["Working without a plan","Setting priorities and tracking tasks","Avoiding updates","Doing everything at the last minute"],"answer":"Setting priorities and tracking tasks"},{"id":"event-management-common-l4-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A task list should be reviewed and updated as work progresses.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-common-l4-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Arranging tasks from most to least important is called ______.","answer":"prioritizing"},{"id":"event-management-common-l4-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"A teammate is behind on a shared task. What is the best action?","options":["Ignore it","Offer help and inform the lead","Complain about it later","Take over without telling anyone"],"answer":"Offer help and inform the lead"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l1-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u1-l1","title":"Introduction to Event Management Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"MICE stands for:","options":["Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions","Music, Ideas, Catering, Events","Meetings, Invitations, Costs, Exhibits","Management, Industry, Culture, Events"],"answer":"Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions"},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A wedding is an example of a social event.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The person responsible for the overall planning of an event is the event ______.","answer":"planner"},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Which role coordinates suppliers on the event day?","options":["Event coordinator","Guest","Photographer","Sponsor"],"answer":"Event coordinator"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l2-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u1-l2","title":"Event Conceptualization & Theming Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"A mood board is used to:","options":["Track the budget","Communicate the visual direction","List suppliers","Record attendance"],"answer":"Communicate the visual direction"},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"The event concept should reflect the client's objectives and audience.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The overall visual and emotional direction of an event is its ______.","answer":"theme"},{"id":"event-management-core-u1-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"What should guide the concept of a corporate launch?","options":["The planner's personal taste","The client's brand and goals","The cheapest supplier","The venue's wallpaper"],"answer":"The client's brand and goals"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l1-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u2-l1","title":"Event Budgeting Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which is a fixed cost in an event budget?","options":["Venue rental","Extra chairs rented on the day","Overtime crew","Emergency repairs"],"answer":"Venue rental"},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A budget includes a contingency line for unexpected costs.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The amount set aside for unexpected expenses is the ______.","answer":"contingency"},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Why should expenses be tracked during the event?","options":["To avoid overspending","To delay payments","To raise supplier rates","To reduce attendance"],"answer":"To avoid overspending"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l2-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u2-l2","title":"Venue & Supplier Coordination Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Which factor matters most when choosing a venue?","options":["Capacity and accessibility for guests","The color of the walls","Distance from the planner's home","Free parking for staff only"],"answer":"Capacity and accessibility for guests"},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Supplier contracts should state deliverables, deadlines and payment terms.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The document that binds a supplier to deliver services is a ______.","answer":"contract"},{"id":"event-management-core-u2-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Why is a site visit done?","options":["To confirm layout and logistics","To sign the guest list","To choose the menu only","To pay the deposit only"],"answer":"To confirm layout and logistics"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l1-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u3-l1","title":"Program Flow & Stage Management Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"A program flow is:","options":["A minute-by-minute schedule of activities","A list of guests","The venue map","The budget summary"],"answer":"A minute-by-minute schedule of activities"},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"Cues are coordinated with the technical team before the event.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"The person who signals lights and sound cues is the stage ______.","answer":"manager"},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"Why are time buffers built into a program flow?","options":["To fill empty time","To absorb delays","To lengthen the event","To reduce costs"],"answer":"To absorb delays"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l2-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u3-l2","title":"Event Day Operations Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l2-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"Registration desks should be:","options":["Hidden from guests","Clearly signposted and staffed","Closed until noon","Manned by suppliers only"],"answer":"Clearly signposted and staffed"},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l2-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A contingency plan should cover bad weather and supplier no-shows.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l2-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Directing guests to their seats is called ______.","answer":"ushering"},{"id":"event-management-core-u3-l2-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"What is the first action when a supplier fails to arrive?","options":["Cancel the event","Activate the contingency plan and inform the client","Argue with the supplier","Leave the venue"],"answer":"Activate the contingency plan and inform the client"}]},{"id":"event-management-core-u4-l1-quiz","programId":"event-management","lessonId":"event-management-core-u4-l1","title":"Post-Event Reporting Quiz","passing":75,"timeLimit":15,"published":true,"questions":[{"id":"event-management-core-u4-l1-quiz-q1","type":"mcq","q":"A post-event report usually contains:","options":["Attendance, financials and feedback","Photos only","The guest list only","Supplier contacts only"],"answer":"Attendance, financials and feedback"},{"id":"event-management-core-u4-l1-quiz-q2","type":"tf","q":"A client debrief helps identify improvements for future events.","answer":true},{"id":"event-management-core-u4-l1-quiz-q3","type":"id","q":"Gathering client comments after an event is called collecting ______.","answer":"feedback"},{"id":"event-management-core-u4-l1-quiz-q4","type":"mcq","q":"When should the post-event report be delivered?","options":["Within an agreed short period after the event","Six months later","Before the event","Only if the client asks"],"answer":"Within an agreed short period after the event"}]}]$q$::jsonb)
  where id = 'event-management';

